        <h2>Overview</h2>

        <p>
            The Mothman is a famous American cryptid and is notoriously tied to local disasters and paranormal folklore.
        </p>

        <h2>Appearance</h2>

        <p>
            Witnesses describe the Mothman to be a 6 to 7-foot-tall humanoid creature with red glowing eyes 
            and bat-like wings.
        </p>

        <h2>Habitat</h2>

        <p>
            The Mothman does not have a specified habitat, but is commonly tied to: Overgrown Woodlands and 
            Abandoned Infrastructure
        </p>

        <h2>Reported sightings</h2>

        <ul>
            <li>It was first sighted in Point Pleasant, West Virginia, between 1966 and 1967.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Theories</h2>

        <p>
            Some believe the sightings were simply misidentified sandhill cranes-a tall bird with a wide wingspan and red circles around
            its eyes. While others believe it could be linked to paranormal activity and supernatural curses.
        </p>

